@w.lang.en.construction.neg.rule.same w.lang.en.construction name=neg.rule.same doc="a rewrite of a sentence (normalizer, paraphrase, correction) must keep the negation: both or neither carry one; stop / undo / cancel are not negations here" core.source="psys2 78f45863"
@w.lang.en.construction.neg.rule.aux w.lang.en.construction name=neg.rule.aux doc="negation of a statement ('Ion does not eat 1 apple': the worlds' neg patterns, kids.arith kids.shop) is read by the worlds; negation of a REQUEST is read here (slice 2): the sentence opens with the lead words of neg.imperative and is not carried out" core.source="psys2 78f45863"
@w.lang.en.construction.imperative.rule w.lang.en.construction name=imperative.rule function=grammar.read doc="the verb of a request is the words before the first determiner, number, pronoun or preposition (at most 3, lead-in words removed): the first word of an imperative sentence" core.source="psys2 78f45863"
